{title: 212 - 'Tis Almost Time for the Lord to Come}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #212 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 212}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]'Tis almost time for the [Gb]Lord to come, I [Db]hear the people [Ab]say;
[Ab]The [Db]stars of heav[Ab7]en[D]are [Gb]growing dim, It [Db]must be the [Ab]breaking [Ab7]of the [Db]day.
[Db]O it must be the breaking of the day! O it [Ab]must be the breaking of the [Db]day!
[Db]The night is almost gone, The [Gb]day is coming [Db]on;
[Db]O it must [Gb]be the [Ab]breaking [Ab7]of the [Db]day!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Db]O it [Gb]must be [Db]the breaking [Ab]of the day!
[Ab]O [Db]it [Ab7]must [D]be [Gb]the [Db]breaking [Ab]of [Ab7]the [Db]day!
[Db]The [Ab]night is [Db]almost gone,
[Db]The [Gb]day is [Db]coming on;
[Db]O [Gb]it must [Ab]be the [Ab7]breaking of [Db]the day!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]The signs [Gb]foretold in [Db]the sun [Ab]and moon,
[Ab][Db]In [Ab7]earth [D][Gb]and [Db]sea [Ab][Ab7]and [Db]sky,
[Db]Aloud [Ab]proclaim to [Db]all mankind,
[Db]The coming [Gb]of the [Db]Master draweth nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]It must [Gb]be time [Db]for the [Ab]waiting church
[Ab][Db]To [Ab7][D]cast [Gb][Db]her [Ab][Ab7]pride [Db]away,
[Db]With girded [Ab]loins and [Db]burning lamps,
[Db]To look [Gb]for the breaking [Db]of the day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db]Go quickly [Gb]out in [Db]the streets [Ab]and lanes
[Ab][Db]And [Ab7][D]in [Gb][Db]the [Ab][Ab7]broad [Db]highway,
[Db]And call [Ab]the maimed, the [Db]halt, and blind,
[Db]To be ready [Gb]for the breaking [Db]of the day.
{end_of_verse}
